          {
            "typeName": "originOfSources",
            "multiple": false,
            "typeClass": "primitive",
            "value": "Gini version 3, please see documentation here:\nhttps://www.gapminder.org/data/documentation/gini/\nGDP per capita in constant PPP dollars version 31, see documentation here:\nhttp://gapminder.org/data/documentation/gd001/\nPopulation by country, see documentation here:\nhttps://www.gapminder.org/data/documentation/gd003/\nFor countries that gapminder did not have population information for, World Bank dataset was used:\nhttps://data.worldbank.org/indicator/SP.POP.TOTL\nDataset used to get athlete death dates, birth dates and other individual characteristics from Olympedia. This is more correct than the original dataset:\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/datasets/vaibhav1056/olympics-athletes-born-data\n\nDataset web scraped from Olympedia, used to add latitude, longitude, places obtained in Olympics, whether the result was a tie and all other non-economic data columns. Also used to double check whether data obtained from olympedia web scraped athlete characteristics file (above) is correct:\nhttps://github.com/KeithGalli/Olympics-Dataset/tree/master"
          }
